Virtual DOM

The Virtual DOM is a lightweight representation of the actual browser DOM.

When your React application changes, React:

Creates an updated Virtual DOM.
Compares it with the previous Virtual DOM.
Finds what changed.
Updates only the necessary parts of the real DOM.
Simple example
